      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-333809",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x):$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{\u2032}=2x+y+3z,\\, & y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{\u2032}=x-y+2z,\\, & z(0)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $\u0394y$ and $\u0394z$ in the table below if the step size is $\u0394x=\\frac{1}{4}?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{\u2032}$ | $\u0394y$ | $z$ | ${z}^{\u2032}$ | $\u0394z$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |\n\nTherefore, $y\\,(\\frac{1}{4})\u2248$\n{{field-3}}\nand $z\\,(\\frac{1}{4})\u2248$\n{{field-4}}."
    }
